{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in specifications. The policy gives priority to move_forward in clear conditions, uses random_walk only as a secondary exploration bias, routes every obstacle observation through a dedicated recovery state, prefers short directed turns for side obstacles, uses a rare one-shot backward escape only for front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion with compact plant automata.",
    "Use one policy specification with perception and one-shot action states so each non-decision state enables exactly one controllable action.",
    "Bias strongly toward forward progress by returning to forward exploration immediately on path_clear after recovery.",
    "Use rotate_clockwise for left-obstacle recovery and rotate_counterclockwise for right-obstacle recovery consistently.",
    "Allow full_rotate only from a dedicated stuck state reached after repeated front-blocked recovery failures."
  ],
